    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d376">

                <pb facs="0905" n="860" sameAs="frus:frus1977-80v19/pg860"/>

                <head>376. Telegram From the Embassy in Pakistan to the Department of State and the
                    Consulate in Karachi<anchor n="1" xml:id="d376-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Islamabad</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1979-11-21T08:30:00+00:00">November 21, 1979,
                        0830Z</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>13177. 1. At approximately 1245 local time about 330 students, Pakistani and
                    Iranian, from Quaid-i-Azam University in Islamabad, began a demonstration in
                    front of the Embassy. They left briefly, but then, joined by four more busloads,
                    returned. The compound is fairly well protected; students have breached the
                    grounds. Local police are, however, firing shots into the air and tear gas is
                    being used. We have asked for more police.</p>
                <p>2. The protesters are shouting slogans against Carter and an alleged American takeover of the Qabba in
                        Mecca.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d376-f2"/> They have burned an Embassy vehicle.
                    More reports later.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Hummel</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
